ned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -5 & 4 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4\\cdot (-7)-(-6)\\cdot (-2))i-((-5)\\cdot (-7)-(-6)\\cdot (-1))j+((-5)\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =-40i-29j+14k \\\\  & =⟨-40,-29,14⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-40)^{2}+(-29)^{2}+{14}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2637} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{293}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{293}}{2}.\n$$" 13194139535828 17592186045443 true] [17592186530787 1080 "11" 13194139535828 17592186045443 true] [17592186530787 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535828 17592186045443 true] [17592186530787 1083 #uuid "1c91fca4-1a47-542b-92ef-c0df31262767" 13194139535828 17592186045443 true] [17592186530788 1080 "\\sqrt{3493}" 13194139535828 17592186045443 true] [17592186530788 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535828 17592186045443 true] [17592186530788 1083 #uuid "1f716af9-0180-5b87-b139-f9ae40fa13c3" 13194139535828 17592186045443 true] [17592186530789 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530781 13194139535828 17592186045443 true] [17592186530789 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535828 17592186045443 true] [17592186530789 1071 "Calculate the area of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(-1,4,-2)$, $B(0,2,-2)$, $C(-1,2,-3).$" 13194139535828 17592186045443 true] [17592186530789 1072 #uuid "1fc0d6d3-68d3-53c1-9126-183c39fa054f" 13194139535828 17592186045443 true] [17592186530789 1074 "